You don't need a package for this. Just `await` won't help, as it only drains microtasks, so timers like your `tick()` never get a chance to run. You need to yield to the event loop with `setImmediate`:

```js
import {setImmediate} from 'node:timers/promises';

let lastYield = performance.now();

for (const item of items) {
	process(item);

	if (performance.now() - lastYield > 50) {
		await setImmediate();
		lastYield = performance.now();
	}
}
```

Works the same inside a `pEachSeries` iterator. There's also `scheduler.yield()` in `node:timers/promises`, but it's still experimental.

